{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isAlpha\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isAlpha</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if alphabetic character\n\nGenerated by `General_Category=L | General_Category=Nl | Other_Alphabetic`.\n\nUnicode property: `Alphabetic` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isAlpha","kind":"def","line":1023,"name":"Unicode.isAlpha","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L1023-L1024"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isAlphabetic\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isAlphabetic</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if alphabetic character\n\nGenerated by `General_Category=L | General_Category=Nl | Other_Alphabetic`.\n\nUnicode property: `Alphabetic` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isAlphabetic","kind":"def","line":1010,"name":"Unicode.isAlphabetic","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L1010-L1021"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isMath\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isMath</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if mathematical symbol character\n\nGenerated by `General_Category=Sm | Other_Math`.\n\nUnicode property: `Math` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isMath","kind":"def","line":1002,"name":"Unicode.isMath","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L1002-L1008"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isWhiteSpace\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isWhiteSpace</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if white space character\n\nUnicode property: `White_Space`\n","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isWhiteSpace","kind":"def","line":989,"name":"Unicode.isWhiteSpace","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L989-L1000"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isDefaultIgnorableCodePoint\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isDefaultIgnorableCodePoint</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if default ignorable character\n\nUnicode property: `Default_Ignorable_Code_Point`\n","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isDefaultIgnorableCodePoint","kind":"def","line":981,"name":"Unicode.isDefaultIgnorableCodePoint","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L981-L987"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isNoncharacterCodePoint\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isNoncharacterCodePoint</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if noncharacter code point\n\nUnicode property: `Noncharacter_Code_Point`\n","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isNoncharacterCodePoint","kind":"def","line":973,"name":"Unicode.isNoncharacterCodePoint","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L973-L979"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getHexDigit?\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getHexDigit?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Fin\">Fin</a> <span class=\"fn\">16</span>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Get value of a hexadecimal digit\n\nReturns `none` if the character is not a hexadecimal digit in the sense of\n`isHexDigit`. Both ASCII and fullwidth forms are accepted.\n\nUnicode property: `Hex_Digit` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getHexDigit?","kind":"def","line":944,"name":"Unicode.getHexDigit?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L944-L967"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isHexDigit\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isHexDigit</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if character represents a hexadecimal digit\n\nUnicode property: `Hex_Digit` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isHexDigit","kind":"def","line":931,"name":"Unicode.isHexDigit","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L931-L942"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getDecimalRange?\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getDecimalRange?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> (<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Get decimal digit range\n\nIf the character is part of a contiguous sequence representing the ten\ndecimal digits in order from 0 to 9, this function returns the first and\nlast characters from this range.\n\nUnicode properties:\n  `Numeric_Type=Decimal`\n  `Numeric_Value` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getDecimalRange?","kind":"def","line":907,"name":"Unicode.getDecimalRange?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L907-L929"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isDecimal\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isDecimal</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if character represents a decimal digit\n\nFor this property, a character must be part of a contiguous sequence\nrepresenting the ten decimal digits in order from 0 to 9.\n\nUnicode property: `Numeric_Type=Decimal` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isDecimal","kind":"def","line":891,"name":"Unicode.isDecimal","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L891-L905"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getDigit?\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getDigit?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Fin\">Fin</a> <span class=\"fn\">10</span>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Get value of digit\n\nReturns `none` if the character is not a digit in the sense of `isDigit`.\n\nUnicode properties:\n`Numeric_Type=Decimal | Numeric_Type=Digit`\n`Numeric_Value` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getDigit?","kind":"def","line":866,"name":"Unicode.getDigit?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L866-L889"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isDigit\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isDigit</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if character represents a digit in base 10\n\nThis includes decimal digits as well as other digits such as U+00B2\nSUPERSCRIPT TWO.\n\nUnicode property: `Numeric_Type=Decimal | Numeric_Type=Digit` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isDigit","kind":"def","line":849,"name":"Unicode.isDigit","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L849-L864"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isNumeric\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isNumeric</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if character represents a numerical value\n\nThis includes decimal digits and other digits.\n\nUnicode property: `Numeric_Type` (any value other than `None`) ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isNumeric","kind":"def","line":814,"name":"Unicode.isNumeric","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L814-L847"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getDecompositionMapping?\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getDecompositionMapping?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./UnicodeBasic/Types.html#Unicode.DecompositionMapping\">DecompositionMapping</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Get decomposition mapping of a character\n\nReturns `none` if the character has no decomposition mapping. The `tag`\nfield is `none` for a canonical mapping and `some _` for a compatibility\nmapping. This is a single decomposition step, not the full decomposition\nused in normalization to canonical decomposition (`NFD`) and compatibility\ndecomposition (`NFKD`).\n\nUnicode properties:\n  `Decomposition_Type`\n  `Decomposition_Mapping` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getDecompositionMapping?","kind":"def","line":792,"name":"Unicode.getDecompositionMapping?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L792-L808"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getCanonicalDecomposition\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getCanonicalDecomposition</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Get full canonical decomposition of character (`NFD`)\n\nReturns the full canonical decomposition of the character, including for\nHangul syllables. Returns the character itself if it has no canonical\ndecomposition.\n\nUnicode properties:\n  `Decomposition_Mapping`\n  `Decomposition_Type=Canonical` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getCanonicalDecomposition","kind":"def","line":778,"name":"Unicode.getCanonicalDecomposition","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L778-L790"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getCanonicalCombiningClass\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getCanonicalCombiningClass</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Get canonical combining class of character\n\nCharacters with combining class `0` are called starters. These include all\ncharacters that are not combining marks, as well as some combining marks.\n\nUnicode property: `Canonical_Combining_Class`\n","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getCanonicalCombiningClass","kind":"def","line":764,"name":"Unicode.getCanonicalCombiningClass","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L764-L776"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.matchPrefixCaseInsensitive?\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">matchPrefixCaseInsensitive?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">pat </span><span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/String/Defs.html#String.Slice\">String.Slice</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> (<a href=\"./Init/Data/String/Defs.html#String.Slice\">String.Slice</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Init/Data/String/Defs.html#String.Slice\">String.Slice</a>)</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Case-insensitive prefix match\n\nIf `pat` matches a prefix of `s` up to full case folding, returns that prefix\nand the rest of `s`. Otherwise, returns `none`. For example, `\"straße\"`\nmatches `\"STRASSE\"`, but `\"ß\"` does not match `\"S\"`, since the full case\nfolding of `\"ß\"` is `\"ss\"`.\n\nThis is default caseless matching, as defined in the Unicode Standard; it\ndoes not normalize either string.\n\nUnicode property: `Case_Folding` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.matchPrefixCaseInsensitive?","kind":"def","line":715,"name":"Unicode.matchPrefixCaseInsensitive?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L715-L758"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getCaseFolding\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getCaseFolding</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Full case folding of a character\n\nThe result may consist of more than one character, for example `\"ss\"` for\nU+00DF LATIN SMALL LETTER SHARP S.\n\nUnicode property: `Case_Folding` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getCaseFolding","kind":"def","line":705,"name":"Unicode.getCaseFolding","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L705-L713"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.withCaseFolding\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">withCaseFolding</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Sort</a> u_1}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a></span> → <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Full case folding of a character, in continuation-passing style\n\nCalls `k` with the first character of the full case folding of `char` and\nthe list of its remaining characters. For example, for U+00DF LATIN SMALL\nLETTER SHARP S, `k` is called with `'s'` and `['s']`.\n\nUnicode property: `Case_Folding` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.withCaseFolding","kind":"def","line":693,"name":"Unicode.withCaseFolding","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L693-L703"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getCaseFoldingChar\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getCaseFoldingChar</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Simple case folding of a character\n\nReturns the character itself if it has no case folding. This function does\nnot handle the case where case folding would consist of more than one\ncharacter; use `getCaseFolding` for full case folding.\n\nUnicode property: `Simple_Case_Folding` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getCaseFoldingChar","kind":"def","line":660,"name":"Unicode.getCaseFoldingChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L660-L677"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getTitle\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getTitle</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Full titlecase mapping of a character\n\nThe result may consist of more than one character, for example `\"Ss\"` for\nU+00DF LATIN SMALL LETTER SHARP S. Conditional mappings are not applied.\n\nUnicode property: `Titlecase_Mapping` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getTitle","kind":"def","line":651,"name":"Unicode.getTitle","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L651-L658"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.withTitlecasing\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">withTitlecasing</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Sort</a> u_1}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a></span> → <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Full titlecase mapping of a character, in continuation-passing style\n\nCalls `k` with the first character of the full titlecase mapping of `char`\nand the list of its remaining characters. For example, for U+00DF LATIN SMALL\nLETTER SHARP S, `k` is called with `'S'` and `['s']`. Conditional mappings\nare not applied.\n\nUnicode property: `Titlecase_Mapping` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.withTitlecasing","kind":"def","line":638,"name":"Unicode.withTitlecasing","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L638-L649"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getTitleChar\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getTitleChar</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Map character to titlecase\n\nReturns the character itself if it has no titlecase mapping. This function\ndoes not handle the case where the full titlecase mapping would consist of\nmore than one character, for example U+00DF LATIN SMALL LETTER SHARP S; use\n`getTitle` for the full titlecase mapping.\n\nUnicode property: `Simple_Titlecase_Mapping` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getTitleChar","kind":"def","line":604,"name":"Unicode.getTitleChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L604-L621"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getUpper\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getUpper</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Full uppercase mapping of a character\n\nThe result may consist of more than one character, for example `\"SS\"` for\nU+00DF LATIN SMALL LETTER SHARP S. Conditional mappings are not applied.\n\nUnicode property: `Uppercase_Mapping` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getUpper","kind":"def","line":595,"name":"Unicode.getUpper","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L595-L602"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.withUppercasing\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">withUppercasing</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Sort</a> u_1}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a></span> → <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Full uppercase mapping of a character, in continuation-passing style\n\nCalls `k` with the first character of the full uppercase mapping of `char`\nand the list of its remaining characters. For example, for U+00DF LATIN SMALL\nLETTER SHARP S, `k` is called with `'S'` and `['S']`. Conditional mappings\nare not applied.\n\nUnicode property: `Uppercase_Mapping` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.withUppercasing","kind":"def","line":582,"name":"Unicode.withUppercasing","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L582-L593"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getUpperChar\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getUpperChar</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Map character to uppercase\n\nReturns the character itself if it has no uppercase mapping. This function\ndoes not handle the case where the full uppercase mapping would consist of\nmore than one character, for example U+00DF LATIN SMALL LETTER SHARP S; use\n`getUpper` for the full uppercase mapping.\n\nUnicode property: `Simple_Uppercase_Mapping` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getUpperChar","kind":"def","line":548,"name":"Unicode.getUpperChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L548-L565"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getLower\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getLower</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Full lowercase mapping of a character\n\nThe result may consist of more than one character, for example `\"i\\u0307\"`\nfor U+0130 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER I WITH DOT ABOVE. Conditional mappings, such\nas for final sigma, are not applied.\n\nUnicode property: `Lowercase_Mapping` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getLower","kind":"def","line":538,"name":"Unicode.getLower","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L538-L546"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.withLowercasing\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">withLowercasing</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Sort</a> u_1}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a></span> → <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Full lowercase mapping of a character, in continuation-passing style\n\nCalls `k` with the first character of the full lowercase mapping of `char`\nand the list of its remaining characters. For example, for U+0130 LATIN\nCAPITAL LETTER I WITH DOT ABOVE, `k` is called with `'i'` and `['\\u0307']`.\nConditional mappings, such as for final sigma, are not applied.\n\nUnicode property: `Lowercase_Mapping` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.withLowercasing","kind":"def","line":525,"name":"Unicode.withLowercasing","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L525-L536"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getLowerChar\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">getLowerChar</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Map character to lowercase\n\nReturns the character itself if it has no lowercase mapping. This function\ndoes not handle the case where the full lowercase mapping would consist of\nmore than one character, for example U+0130 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER I WITH DOT ABOVE;\nuse `getLower` for the full lowercase mapping.\n\nUnicode property: `Simple_Lowercase_Mapping` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.getLowerChar","kind":"def","line":490,"name":"Unicode.getLowerChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L490-L508"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isCaseIgnorable\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isCaseIgnorable</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if character is ignorable for casing purposes\n\nGenerated from general categories `Lm`, `Mn`, `Me`, `Sk`, `Cf`, and word\nbreak property values `MidLetter`, `MidNumLet`, `Single_Quote`.\n\nUnicode property: `Case_Ignorable` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isCaseIgnorable","kind":"def","line":458,"name":"Unicode.isCaseIgnorable","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L458-L488"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isCased\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isCased</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if cased character\n\nThis includes some characters that are not letters, such as U+24B6 CIRCLED\nLATIN CAPITAL LETTER A.\n\nGenerated by `General_Category=LC | Other_Lowercase | Other_Uppercase`.\n\nUnicode property: `Cased` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isCased","kind":"def","line":442,"name":"Unicode.isCased","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-basic/blob/6e48acac3a91665fcdc4a20d50b7ce6b7b41711f/UnicodeBasic.lean#L442-L456"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isUppercase\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">isUppercase</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">char</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Check if uppercase character\n\nThis includes some characters that are not letters, such as U+24B6 CIRCLED\nLATIN CAPITAL LETTER A.\n\nGenerated by `General_Category=Lu | Other_Uppercase`.\n\nUnicode property: `Uppercase` ","docLink":"./UnicodeBasic.html#Unicode.isUppercase",